          "eyebrow": "recap",
          "title": "What You've Learned",
          "lede": "Three concepts, one workflow: create a Figure, size it, and plot onto its Axes.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_viz_figures_layout_plotting.s13.b01",
              "role": "takeaway",
              "text": "With `plt.subplots()` you get a Figure and an Axes first, then call a plotting method on the Axes, not the Figure. Figure is the canvas; Axes is where data goes. Set `figsize` to control canvas dimensions and call `tight_layout()` to prevent labels from clipping.",
              "lineage": {
