              "role": "definition",
              "text": "The Figure is the outer canvas \u2014 the whole window. The Axes is the inner plotting area where data is drawn. `fig, ax = plt.subplots()` creates both at once: `fig` is the canvas, `ax` is the plotting area. Plotting calls like `ax.plot(x, y)` go on `ax`, never on `fig`.",
